Important Design Concept

The final website must NOT use a traditional navigation bar or menu.

Instead, navigation must be controlled by an AI Navigation Agent (LOGIC) that receives prompts from the user and redirects them to the appropriate page.

Users interact with the website through a chat interface.

Example user prompts:

"I want to learn machine learning"

"Show me your AI courses"

"Who are your instructors?"

"How can I contact you?"

The AI agent determines the intent and navigates to the correct page.

LOGIC Navigation Agent

The frontend includes a LogicAgent component which must remain the primary navigation system.

The agent communicates with:

POST /api/logic/chat

Request format

{
  message: string,
  history: Message[]
}

Response format

{
  text: string,
  intent: string,
  course_id?: number
}

Possible intents:

courses
course_detail
about
contact
home

Navigation behavior:

courses → /courses

course_detail → /courses/{id}

about → /about

contact → scroll to contact section

home → /

The existing LogicAgent React component must remain functional and may be improved but not broken.

